TV VNC — GPL-3.0-or-later

Source code and build instructions: https://github.com/amersheeny/tvvnc

The app links LibVNCClient from LibVNCServer (GPL-2.0-or-later), pinned by
the native/libvncserver Git submodule. Its copyright and license notices remain
in that dependency's COPYING and AUTHORS files.
The maintained fork marks its 2026-09-21 socket-read and monotonic timeout
modifications in source and TVCONSOLE_CHANGES.md; it is not unmodified upstream.
That historical filename retains the project's earlier name for traceability.

JPEG decoding uses libjpeg-turbo, pinned by native/libjpeg-turbo. Its component
licenses and attribution are in that dependency's LICENSE.md.
This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.

Android TV control uses the androidtv-remote library extracted in a maintained
ScreenCast fork (Apache-2.0), pinned by native/androidtv-remote. Upstream history,
license and modification notices remain in the dependency repository. Generated
protocol messages use androidtvremote2's Apache-2.0 schemas, pinned by its nested
protocol-schemas submodule.

Protocol Buffers Java Lite uses the BSD-3-Clause license bundled in
assets/licenses/protobuf-LICENSE.txt. Its source is available at
https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/tree/v36.2.

Sony encrypted-text interoperability was cross-checked against the documented
Sony API and Brandon Dusseau's braviaproapi Encryption implementation (MIT).
No braviaproapi source is included in this application.

Bounded, cancellable Sony HTTP requests use OkHttp 5.5.0 (Apache-2.0),
published as com.squareup.okhttp3:okhttp. Its upstream source and license are
available at https://github.com/lysine-dev/okhttp.

OkHttp includes Public Suffix List data under Mozilla Public License 2.0,
bundled in assets/licenses/MPL-2.0.txt. The list's source and license are at
https://publicsuffix.org/list/ and the OkHttp release source at
https://github.com/lysine-dev/okhttp/tree/parent-5.5.0.

Okio, Kotlin standard library, Kotlin coroutines, JetBrains annotations,
AndroidX and Guava ListenableFuture are distributed under Apache-2.0, whose
license text is bundled at native/androidtv-remote/LICENSE. Flutter and Dart
dependency notices are supplied in Flutter's NOTICES.Z asset.

No analytics, advertising SDK, cloud relay or VPN engine is included in Phase 0.
